From: uf maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Admit React 19 async component results in the bundled Flow library

Issue: https://github.com/ubugeeei-prod/uf/pull/1291
Upstream: not filed yet
Submodule: 81b0c2a3dd591c66c51167aac341d851932bd9c5

React 19 renders promises, but the pinned React$Node union rejects the return
value of an async function component, including RSC functions that await fetch.
Add Promise of the resolved node union without relaxing its props or allowing
arbitrary objects. Async client functions remain unsupported by React; this is
its shared node type, not a promise that a renderer permits async components.
Reference: https://react.dev/reference/rsc/server-components
Regression: crates/uf_check/tests/upstream_patches.rs

--- a/lib/react.js
+++ b/lib/react.js
@@ -12,7 +12,11 @@
  * addition to elements and arrays of nodes.
  */
 
-declare type React$Node =
+declare type React$Node = React$AwaitedNode | Promise<React$AwaitedNode>;
+
+// Promise resolution is renderable in React 19, including async Server Components.
+// Keep the resolved union separate: Promise<React$Node> recursively awaits itself.
+declare type React$AwaitedNode =
   | void
   | null
   | boolean
